{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Java code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Java 8 code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Java 8 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Solution {\n    private static BufferedReader br;\n    private static StringTokenizer st;\n    private static PrintWriter pw;\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {\n        br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        pw = new PrintWriter(System.out);\n        solve();\n        pw.close();\n    }\n\n    private static void solve() throws IOException {\n        int a = parseInt(), b = parseInt();\n        int left = parseInt() - 1, right = parseInt() - 1;\n        int len = right - left + 1;\n        int best = len;\n\n        for (char c1 = 'a'; c1 <= 'z'; c1++) {\n            for (char c2 = 'a'; c2 <= 'z'; c2++) {\n                for (char c3 = 'a'; c3 <= 'z'; c3++) {\n                    best = Math.min(best, distinctInSegment(a, b, left, right, new char[]{c1, c2, c3}));\n                }\n            }\n        }\n\n        pw.println(best);\n    }\n\n    private static int distinctInSegment(int a, int b, int l, int r, char[] p) {\n        int period = a + b;\n        char[] full = new char[3 * period];\n        for (int i = 0; i < 3; i++) {\n            char[] prefix = prefixPattern(full, i * period, a);\n            System.arraycopy(prefix, 0, full, i * period, a);\n            Arrays.fill(full, i * period + a, (i + 1) * period, p[i]);\n        }\n\n        int start = l % period;\n        int n = r - l + 1;\n        char[] window = new char[n];\n        System.arraycopy(full, start, window, 0, Math.min(n, full.length - start));\n\n        int[] freq = new int[26];\n        for (char c : window) freq[c - 'a']++;\n        int d = 0;\n        for (int f : freq) if (f > 0) d++;\n        return d;\n    }\n\n    private static char[] prefixPattern(char[] buffer, int offset, int len) {\n        boolean[] used = new boolean[26];\n        for (int i = offset - 1; i >= offset - len && i >= 0; i--)\n            used[buffer[i] - 'a'] = true;\n\n        char[] res = new char[len];\n        char cur = 'a';\n        for (int i = 0; i < len; i++) {\n            while (used[cur - 'a']) cur++;\n            res[i] = cur++;\n        }\n        return res;\n    }\n\n    private static int parseInt() throws IOException {\n        return Integer.parseInt(next());\n    }\n\n    private static String next() throws IOException {\n        while (st == null || !st.hasMoreTokens())\n            st = new StringTokenizer(br.readLine());\n        return st.nextToken();\n    }\n\n    private static class StringTokenizer {\n        private String[] tokens;\n        private int index;\n\n        public StringTokenizer(String s) {\n            tokens = s.split(\"\\\\s+\");\n            index = 0;\n        }\n\n        public boolean hasMoreTokens() {\n            return index < tokens.length;\n        }\n\n        public String nextToken() {\n            return tokens[index++];\n        }\n    }\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\nimport io\nimport itertools\n\ndef main():\n    input_data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not input_data:\n        return\n    \n    idx = 0\n    a = int(input_data[idx]); idx += 1\n    b = int(input_data[idx]); idx += 1\n    left = int(input_data[idx]) - 1; idx += 1\n    right = int(input_data[idx]) - 1; idx += 1\n    \n    length = right - left + 1\n    best = length\n    \n    for c1 in map(chr, range(ord('a'), ord('z') + 1)):\n        for c2 in map(chr, range(ord('a'), ord('z') + 1)):\n            for c3 in map(chr, range(ord('a'), ord('z') + 1)):\n                current = distinct_in_segment(a, b, left, right, [c1, c2, c3])\n                if current < best:\n                    best = current\n    \n    print(best)\n\ndef distinct_in_segment(a, b, l, r, p):\n    period = a + b\n    full = [''] * (3 * period)\n    \n    for i in range(3):\n        prefix = prefix_pattern(full, i * period, a)\n        for j in range(a):\n            full[i * period + j] = prefix[j]\n        for j in range(a, period):\n            full[i * period + j] = p[i]\n    \n    start = l % period\n    n = r - l + 1\n    window = []\n    for i in range(n):\n        if start + i < len(full):\n            window.append(full[start + i])\n        else:\n            window.append(full[(start + i) % len(full)])\n    \n    freq = [0] * 26\n    for c in window:\n        freq[ord(c) - ord('a')] += 1\n    \n    d = sum(1 for f in freq if f > 0)\n    return d\n\ndef prefix_pattern(buffer, offset, len_):\n    used = [False] * 26\n    for i in range(offset - 1, offset - len_ - 1, -1):\n        if i >= 0 and i < len(buffer):\n            used[ord(buffer[i]) - ord('a')] = True\n    \n    res = [''] * len_\n    cur = 'a'\n    for i in range(len_):\n        while used[ord(cur) - ord('a')]:\n            cur = chr(ord(cur) + 1)\n        res[i] = cur\n        cur = chr(ord(cur) + 1)\n    return res\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.85\n</confidence>", "token_logprob